# XCU admin
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# SCCS files are made and inspected only with the SCCS utilities (admin,
# get, delta, prs and friends); the file format is unspecified so nothing
# reads the files directly. A missing companion utility makes the test
# UNRESOLVED. Login names, dates and the diagnostic texts are never compared
# literally.

assertion  XCU.admin.001
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/admin.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       admin -iname creates s.name from the text of a file as the first
           delta, the new file has no write permission, no x-file or z-file
           is left, and get returns the same text.
test       t/001-create-from-file.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.002
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/admin.html#STDIN
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -n creates a file with no text and -i without a name reads the
           text from standard input.
test       t/002-empty-and-stdin.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.003
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -r3 makes the initial delta 3.1 and the level defaults to 1.
test       t/003-initial-release.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.004
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       The m, t, q, b, j, c, f, n, d and i flags set with -f are
           reflected by prs, the default module name is the file name
           without s., and -d removes b and j.
test       t/004-flags.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.005
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -tname stores descriptive text, -t alone removes it from an
           existing file, -y sets the comment of the initial delta, and the
           default comment starts with the creation text.
test       t/005-description-comment.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.006
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -a adds login names to the list of users who may make deltas and
           -e removes them.
test       t/006-user-list.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.007
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -h passes an intact file silently, reports a damaged one, and -z
           recomputes the checksum so that -h passes again.
test       t/007-check-and-sum.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.008
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/admin.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A single - operand reads SCCS file names from standard input; an
           unreadable -i file gives a non-zero status and creates nothing.
test       t/008-operands-and-errors.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.009
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS/-f
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS/-d
class      required
since      1992
says       The l flag with a release list (or a) makes get -e of a locked
           release fail, and -d with the l flag unlocks it.
test       t/009-lock-flag.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.010
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS/-f
class      required
since      1992
says       The j flag allows a second get -e on the same SID while the first
           edit is outstanding.
test       t/010-joint-edit-flag.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.011
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       A directory operand applies the operation to every SCCS file in it
           and silently ignores other files.
test       t/011-directory-operand.sh

assertion  XCU.admin.012
anchor     utilities/admin.html#OPTIONS/-m
class      required
since      1992
says       With the v flag set, -m records MR numbers for the initial delta
           of a new file; without the v flag, a diagnostic is written.
test       t/012-mr-initial.sh
